{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/398226-what-the-charlatans-can-do","id":398226,"title":"What the Charlatans can do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-08T17:25:58-08:00","id":398226,"title":"What the Charlatans can do?","content":"In my nearest game session I want to make a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/342038-masquerade-ball-murder\">plot with Exiled Charlatan</a>. He want to confront the PCs and &quot;make them&quot; to help him. But first and foremost, he invites them on his masqueraded ball. So here are quick questions about the powers of Charlatans in <b>Changeling</b>.<br /> <br /> 1, I assume the Charlatans are stated like powerful changelings, yes? They have Wyrd, Contracts and all alike. Is there something special in their power? What things they can use outside of normal Lost scope?<br /> <br /> 2. The key to the plot is making PCs locked in the ball room. That mean no hoping to the Hedge - is there in system any Contract or other power that is temporary shutting the ability to open Portals to it in area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T19:13:04-08:00","id":399760,"title":"","content":"1) The core book presents Charlatans as powerful changelings and Equinox Roads says their rare enough you can really just do whatever because they'll likely be a one of a kind in the chronicle anyway. Autumn Nightmares has a whole writeup that makes them suck (can't spend glamour, can't get into the hedge) but I'd avoid that whole book, personally. My recommendation would be to treat Charlatans as powerful changelings. That really gives them plenty of of oomph while still being clearly below the Others they once were.<br /> <br /> 2) There's no easy way to stop a changeling from getting into the hedge. However, getting back out of the hedge requires finding an already existing hedge gate. If the ballroom is in the Charlatan's Hollow and is simply made up to mirror the mundane house all the guest could be lead through a gate at the front door without realizing it as the view through the front door is the same whether it's going into the house or into the hollow. This does run into the problem of changelings not having a mask in the hedge but that's only noticeable if there are mortals around to notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T20:19:53-08:00","id":399868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>helel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/398226-what-the-charlatans-can-do?p=399760#post399760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Autumn Nightmares has a whole writeup that makes them suck (<b>can't spend glamour</b>, can't get into the hedge) but I'd avoid that whole book, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>AN still being the last Changeling book I read\u2026 no, this is false outside a particular nonuniversal context that almost certainly doesn't apply to a Charlatan who's knowingly and actively trying to get back to Faerie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Autumn Nightmares, p88-89, &quot;Game Traits&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 A Charlatan\u2019s mien is much more subtle than that of a normal True Fae. The mien of such a being is only slightly different from the Mask. Minor details look alien and inhuman, but Charlatans are actually harder for changelings to detect than fetches without careful scrutiny. A changeling looking at a Charlatan does not see the obvious disconnect between Mask and mien present with a changeling or one of the Gentry, and noticing the fae details requires a Wits + Intelligence roll.<br /> \u2022 Charlatans retain Contracts and mien blessings. Whether Charlatans remember how to invoke them is up to the Storyteller. In addition, Charlatans can learn and use Echoes, subject to the same prerequisites as fetches (Echoes that usually work only on a given fetch\u2019s changeling \u201cbase\u201d can be applied to any changeling).<br /> \u2022 Likewise, Charlatans can spend Glamour in all of the ways that True Fae can, if they remember how to do so. They regain Glamour normally, except that they cannot regain Glamour by breaking or ripping apart an object.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T20:22:55-08:00","id":399882,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I had misremembered. I must have simply recalled the &quot;can't remember how to use glamour&quot; bit. It's been a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T23:39:43-08:00","id":401522,"title":"","content":"I thought Autumn Nightmares was a really good book m'self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T20:00:16-08:00","id":402850,"title":"","content":"The best of the supplements, I thought myself. Although Dancers in the Dusk may have actually overtaken it in my esteem, it's a tough choice. I adored the extra Fetch information, not to mention all those wonderful Echoes and ideas for what Fetch components might do...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T06:03:35-08:00","id":403231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>helel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/398226-what-the-charlatans-can-do?p=399760#post399760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) There's no easy way to stop a changeling from getting into the hedge. However, getting back out of the hedge requires finding an already existing hedge gate. If the ballroom is in the Charlatan's Hollow and is simply made up to mirror the mundane house all the guest could be lead through a gate at the front door without realizing it as the view through the front door is the same whether it's going into the house or into the hollow. This does run into the problem of changelings not having a mask in the hedge but that's only noticeable if there are mortals around to notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I given &quot;Mask Strengthening&quot; Tokens by the Charlatean with their invitations. He will also use this. Mortals will be on the ball and will be under the spell of &quot;must partying, hear music&quot;. But it's the players that will decide what will be their fate - are people need to die, or will PCs goes in willing slavery for the Charlatan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T09:11:48-08:00","id":403367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/398226-what-the-charlatans-can-do?p=403231#post403231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I given &quot;Mask Strengthening&quot; Tokens by the Charlatean with their invitations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The particular contexts required by a lot of fae magic means usually stuff handed out for the purposes of a single party will only work at that single party. Also\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL1e Core, p211, &quot;Changelings and the Hedge&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, a changeling in the Hedge cannot hide what he is. His mien is visible for all to see, even if a viewer is watching him from outside the Hedge. Indeed, a mortal might stumble upon an open gateway into the Hedge and spy a Bright One bathing or a Beast on the hunt, and feel compelled to follow this strange being or to run home and hide for the next few days. <b>No Contract, token or entitlement allows a changeling to hide his nature in the Hedge.</b> Amidst the Brambles, a changeling cannot help but feel exposed, vulnerable and even trapped, and those feelings are not without merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T23:44:05-08:00","id":404177,"title":"","content":"Read it yesterday, before game session. I went with the idea of Tokens, as they were crucial to make a fine game - because of Rule of Cool - and there is limited number of those in Freehold now, maybe 4 in total. I'm still a bit confused why there is not any Tokens like this officially, for the Others to use - it's nothing game breaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}